{text:"Fix four finitely supported nonnegative sequences x1,x2,x3,x4 on Z\\{0}. Decompose each into shells 2^j<=|k|<2^(j+1), j>=0, and let X_(r,j) be its ell2 norm on shell j. Fix one ordering of shell indices j1>=j2>=j3>=j4 (and correspondingly permute the input labels). Any zero-sum interaction has j1-j2<=2: the largest magnitude is at most three times the second largest, while a gap >=3 would give a ratio greater than four. For each fixed pair of the smaller frequencies, the sum over the two larger frequencies is bounded by the product of their ell2 norms, since one is a translated reflection of the other. Each small shell contains 2^(j+1) integers. Cauchy-Schwarz on the smaller shells therefore bounds the unweighted four-frequency sum by C*2^((j3+j4)/2)*product_r X_(r,jr). Division by N3>=2^j3 leaves C*2^(-(j3-j4)/2).",objects:["x1","x2","x3","x4","Xr","H"],facts:[{id:"F001",statement:"For every ordered shell interaction j1>=j2>=j3>=j4 with j1-j2<=2, its weighted four-linear contribution is at most C*2^(-(j3-j4)/2) product_r X_(r,jr).",objects:["Xr"],assumptions:[]}]},
{text:"Sum F001 with the offset q=j1-j2 in {0,1,2}. Dropping the upper restriction on the small shell indices only increases this positive sum, leaving at most C*(sum_J X_(1,J)X_(2,J-q))*(sum_(ell>=m)2^(-(ell-m)/2)X_(3,ell)X_(4,m)). Interpret negative shell subscripts as zero. Cauchy-Schwarz bounds the first factor by ||X_1||_ell2||X_2||_ell2. In the second set r=ell-m, apply Cauchy-Schwarz to each shifted scalar product, and sum the geometric series: its bound is ||X_3||_ell2||X_4||_ell2/(1-2^(-1/2)). Sum over at most 24 shell orderings and three offsets. Since sum_j X_(r,j)^2=||x_r||_ell2^2, this proves the finite estimate. For arbitrary nonnegative square-summable inputs, restrict all four to |k|<=m. The positive sum is the increasing supremum of these finite sums and the restricted norms are bounded by the original norms; taking the supremum proves the infinite estimate. Restricting the positive summation set can only decrease it.",prev:["F001"],objects:["x1","x2","x3","x4","Xr","H"]}
