{text:"Fix s in [0,1], tau>0, nonnegative n and mean-zero polynomial inputs f1,f2,f3. In each nonzero term of R2 put d=-k, p=a+b, A=|ab|, B0=|cd| and order the four magnitudes. The phase ratios are A/B0 and B0/A. N002 yields |eta|/|k|<=6/N3. Its small-time bound also gives |eta|/(tau|abck|)<=3|p|*min(A,B0)/(A B0)=3|p|/max(A,B0)<=18/N3. The geometric mean with weights 1-s and s is |eta|/(|k|*|abc|^s)<=6^(1-s)*18^s*tau^s/N3. Terms with zero phase or input, or with zero output, contribute zero, so no division by zero is used.",uses:["N002"],objects:["s","tau","n","f1","f2","f3","eta","R2","H"],facts:[{id:"F001",statement:"For every nonzero admissible Fourier term, |eta|/(|k|*|abc|^s)<=6^(1-s)*18^s*tau^s/N3(a,b,c,-k).",binders:[{symbol:"a",type:"integer summation frequency"},{symbol:"b",type:"integer summation frequency"},{symbol:"c",type:"integer summation frequency"},{symbol:"k",type:"integer output frequency"}],objects:["s","tau","eta"],assumptions:[]}]},
