{text:"Use E002 with alpha=0 on an arbitrary I=[a,b] of length <=1, 0<=a<=b. Its input regularity is precisely finite X norm; the source also allows the indicated choice of which slot carries the negative norm. For the time-independent bound use E002 with alpha=s for each s in [0,1]. The source and present Fourier coefficients, phases and projections agree, so its operator C is Cint. Each source L2 and H^r norm is sqrt(2*pi) times ours, and so is its X norm. Dividing either trilinear inequality by sqrt(2*pi) changes only its absolute constant by 2*pi. This proves the two normalized trilinear estimates. Piecewise smooth paths used later satisfy the hypotheses with their weak derivatives; no temporal derivative of a grid jump is introduced because those paths are continuous.",uses:["E002"],objects:["H","Cint","X"]},
