{text:"Fix mean-zero w in H^gamma with ||w||_(H^gamma)<=M, 0<tau<=1 and n>=0. Apply E004 diagonally f=g=w. At beta=a_gamma, the three source lower exponents beta0 are 2*gamma-3/2, -1/2-1/8, gamma-1. Each a_gamma is in [beta0,1+gamma]. The corresponding time powers are (1/2+2*gamma)/(5/2-gamma), 11/17, (1+gamma)/2. In the first case subtracting gamma has numerator (gamma-1/2)(gamma-1)>=0; the other two powers are also >=gamma. Hence tau to that power is <=tau^gamma. At beta=1+gamma the time power is zero. These yield the two asserted bounds, after the same fixed bilinear norm conversion. No norm beyond H^gamma on w was used.",uses:["H002","E004"],objects:["gamma","w","M","tau","n","a_gamma","H","Stage"]}
