{text:"Fix a smooth real mean-zero datum and tau>0. All displayed products and Fourier multipliers preserve smoothness and reality. The F_tau terms have P; the first H_tau term has P, its second is a scalar mean times S_tau Dinv f (which has zero mean), and its endpoint terms have an outer inverse derivative. Thus every iterate is again smooth real and mean zero. For a fixed step set f=S_(-t_n)u^n. Apply E005: v^(n+1)=f+F_n(t_n+tau)+C_n(t_n+tau)-R2_(n,tau)(f,f,f). The maps F_tau,H_tau agree term by term with the selected source edition: the source e^(t partial_x^3) is S_(-t), the source A^n is C_n at the step endpoint, and its R2 is precisely D012 (same -tau/(18*i*k) and phases). This is an algebraic identity for the fixed method, with no convergence theorem invoked.",uses:["E005"],objects:["tau","f","S","P0","P","Dinv","F_tau","H_tau","Psi","R2","B","Stage","Interp"],facts:[{id:"F001",statement:"At each smooth mean-zero step f=S_(-t_n)u^n, v^(n+1)=f+F_n(t_n+tau)+C_n(t_n+tau)-R2_(n,tau)(f,f,f).",objects:["tau","f","S","Psi","R2","Interp"],assumptions:[]}]},
{text:"By Interp, V_n(t_n)=f because all integrals and the affine correction vanish there. At t_n+tau, Q_n cancels the Q_n part of W_n, leaving exactly F001; hence V_n(t_n+tau)=v^(n+1). The pieces concatenate continuously and are piecewise smooth, and Y_n(t_n)=0. Differentiating its explicit formula gives V_n'=B_t(f+F_n,f+F_n)/2-W_n/tau=B_t(z_n,z_n)/2-W_n/tau. Expand V_n=z_n+Y_n by bilinearity and symmetry of B. The difference from B_t(V_n,V_n)/2 is -B_t(Y_n,z_n)-B_t(Y_n,Y_n)/2-W_n/tau, exactly rho_n'. Concatenating increments gives Rres(0)=0 and the asserted equation on each step.",prev:["F001"],objects:["tau","f","Psi","B","Interp"]}
